  "authoringNote": "C09 and C06 regression: every linked receipt is sequenced, so a good receipt never hides another. The order date 2026-09-01 with no timestamp spans 2026-08-31T10:00Z to 2026-09-02T12:00Z, both ends included (C06). Receipt 1 (2026-09-02T17:00:00Z) is after the span and follows the order, so the order has a qualifying receipt and no missing condition holds. Receipt 2 (2026-08-30T15:00:00Z) is before the span start, certainly before the order: R05.receipt_before_order names the order and receipt 2 (conflict, administrative reviewer). Receipt 3 (2026-09-01T20:00:00Z) is inside the span with no order time: R05.receipt_unsequenced names the order and receipt 3 (manual_review, kept beneath the conflict). R05 is conflict, parent set empty, citing three facts of each receipt and the order date (ten). R02 ten; R01 eight, R03 nine, R04 six (pass); R06 five; R07 one. State needs_human_review. The scope batch keeps its ordinary receipt-before-order, equal-instant, unsequenced and missing-receipt cases.",
